  "title": "Commit-message rules reach the commit scan",
  "summary": "Adds a new writing rule, `commit-subject-full-stop`, and a fixed set of `COMMIT_GATE_RULES` (subject full stop, bare reference, reference without label) that the `commit-msg` hook already enforces. The change wires those same gate findings into the two commit-scanning paths — `osf scan --commits` and `osf check scan-commits` — so a pushed commit message is now judged by the same structural rules as a local one, with the rule metadata, docs table and a new integration test covering both paths.",
